WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.619
Hi, it's Paola from Italy.
嗨，我是来自意大利的保拉。

00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:09.560
The first time I watched Alma Mater was during the first wave of COVID that came March 2020.
我第一次看《母校》是在 2020 年 3 月第一波新冠疫情期间。

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.593
My name is Josh.
我叫乔什。

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:14.339
I first watched the show as a college student in New York.
我第一次看这个节目时还是纽约的一名大学生。

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:15.372
My name is Anna.
我叫安娜。

00:00:15.372 --> 00:00:17.568
I am in Los Angeles, planet Earth.
我在地球洛杉矶。

00:00:17.568 --> 00:00:27.772
How I met your mother is special because, whether I've had a fantastic day or a f***ing terrible day, watching that show is always the right move for the mid.
我遇见你母亲的方式很特别，因为无论我度过了美好的一天还是糟糕透顶的一天，观看那个节目始终是中间的正确选择。

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:31.969
My friend told me to watch the show and just said, I'm Ted Mosby.
我的朋友让我看这个节目并只是说，我是特德·莫斯比。

00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:37.770
he's talking about, and I watched it and I came back to him and I said, mm-hmm, I'm dead mostly.
他正在谈论，我看着它，然后我回到他身边，我说，嗯嗯，我基本上已经死了。

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.210
You remember, it was hard time with strict lockdowns, isolation.
你记得，那是一段艰难的时期，严格的封锁和隔离。

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:51.090
After a very tough day, every night, I watched some of my episodes to, let's say, overcome such difficult times.
在经历了非常艰难的一天之后，每天晚上，我都会观看一些剧集，以克服这样的困难时期。

00:00:51.090 --> 00:01:04.689
It feels right, regardless, to go spend time with those characters, those candid, stumbling, hilarious, raunchy, relentlessly then selves people, and that gives the same feeling, the same quality of what good friendship is.
不管怎样，和那些坦率的、跌跌撞撞的、热闹的、不修边幅的、无情的人一起度过时光的感觉是对的，这给了同样的感觉，同样的品质，就像良好的友谊一样。

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:12.489
And being between junior and senior year of college, I was terrified of what was coming next and how to make it happen the way I want.
在大学三年级和四年级之间，我对接下来发生的事情以及如何让它按照我想要的方式发生感到恐惧。

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:21.090
Then there was this wonderful show that was all about how the randomness of life is what gets you exactly where you need to be.
然后有一个精彩的节目，讲述的是生活的随机性如何让你准确地到达你需要去的地方。

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:36.379
I'll be soon in New York City, when I see you.
当我见到你时，我很快就会到纽约。

00:01:36.379 --> 00:01:44.250
Please permit me to tell you everything in New York City.
请允许我告诉你纽约市的一切。

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.650
Well, hello, hello.
嗯，你好，你好。

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.730
This is Josh Radner.
这是乔什·拉德纳。

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:51.290
I am here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我和我的朋友克雷格·托马斯在这里。

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.650
Hi, Josh.
嗨，乔什。

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.090
Hey, it's great to be here with you.
嘿，很高兴和你在一起。

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.250
Welcome to the first episode of How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们如何成就了你的母亲》第一集。

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.969
Are we calling it Wimium?
我们称之为 Wimium 吗？

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:01.969
I was wondering about that, Hwimium.
我很好奇这个问题，Hwimium。

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:02.969
I think it's Hwimium.
我认为是 Hwimium。

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:03.969
Does it work?
有效吗？

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:04.969
I think it does.
我认为确实如此。

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:16.889
So how I make your mother, which is the show under discussion, is a show that ran on CBS from 2005 to 2014, is that right, Craig?
那么，我如何让你的母亲，即正在讨论的节目，成为哥伦比亚广播公司 (CBS) 2005 年至 2014 年播出的节目，对吗，克雷格？

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:18.610
That is correct, nine seasons.
没错，九季。

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:19.449
Nine seasons.
九个季节。

00:02:19.449 --> 00:02:31.050
So almost a decade of our lives, I played the eye in how I make your mother, I played the character of Ted Mosby for nine seasons and Craig tell us what you did on the show.
在我们生命的近十年里，我扮演了如何塑造你母亲的角色，我扮演了泰德·莫斯比这个角色九季，克雷格告诉我们你在剧中做了什么。

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.969
I was Barney.
我是巴尼。

00:02:32.969 --> 00:02:35.050
No, that's right, I remember that.
不，是这样，我记得。

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.169
I have not aged well if you're watching on the YouTube.
如果你在 YouTube 上观看的话，我还没有老好。

00:02:40.169 --> 00:02:48.810
No, I'm the co-creator of the show, along with my very brilliant writing partner, Carter Bees, who will be a guest on here to discuss future and future episodes.
不，我是该剧的共同创作者，还有我非常出色的编剧搭档卡特比斯，他将作为嘉宾在这里讨论未来和未来的剧集。

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:54.370
And we were lucky enough to create the show that found our way to the likes of you, Mr. Ratner.
拉特纳先生，我们很幸运能够制作出这样的节目，并受到了像您这样的人的喜爱。

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.210
Oh, thanks.
哦，谢谢。

00:02:55.210 --> 00:03:01.009
Well, Craig and I have obviously been friends now for coming on two decades, which is astonishing.
嗯，克雷格和我显然已经是二十年来的朋友了，这真是令人惊讶。

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:02.810
We both now live in New York.
我们现在都住在纽约。

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:15.009
About once a year, I would say, we have a habit of grabbing a meal or some drinks and talk inevitably turns to how I made my mother as well as other things that are happening in our lives.
我想说，大约每年一次，我们都有吃顿饭或喝点饮料的习惯，谈话不可避免地会转向我如何创造我的母亲以及我们生活中发生的其他事情。

00:03:15.009 --> 00:03:25.490
But I so enjoy talking about how I made my mother with you and unpacking this thing we made that has been the biggest gift and has carried a lot of shadow with it.
但我非常喜欢谈论我如何与你一起创造我的母亲，并打开我们制作的这个东西的包装，它是最大的礼物，并带有很多阴影。

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:32.090
It's just like all things is a very complicated thing, but also a very beautiful thing.
就好像一切事物都是一件很复杂的事情，但同时也是一件很美好的事情。

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.050
And you're the person I love talking about this show with the most.
你是我最喜欢谈论这个节目的人。

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.849
So when this idea struck me like, you know what?
所以当我想到这个想法时，你知道吗？

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:46.210
It's actually time for me to turn around and revisit how I met your mother but also watch it a lot of the episodes for the first time.
实际上，我是时候回过头来回顾一下我是如何认识你母亲的，但也第一次观看了很多剧集。

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.449
I only watched about half the episodes, what it was on.
我只看了大约一半的剧集，内容是什么。

00:03:48.449 --> 00:03:56.370
So I will be rewatching the show along with you and our listeners, some of whom I assume will be coming to the show for the first time.
因此，我将与您和我们的听众一起重新观看该节目，我认为其中一些人将是第一次观看该节目。

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:01.610
Other ones will have watched it many times and are just looking for the backstage notes here.
其他人可能已经看过很多次了，只是在这里寻找后台笔记。

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:13.810
But I figured if I'm gonna do this, why don't we put it on the record and actually just walk through the show together and much like the older wiser narrator Ted, which we are now around that age.
但我想，如果我要这样做，为什么我们不把它记录下来，实际上只是一起走过这个节目，就像年长而明智的叙述者泰德一样，我们现在已经在这个年纪了。

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.889
Let's look back and see who we were, who we are now, where we're going.
让我们回顾一下，看看我们曾经是谁，现在是谁，我们要去哪里。

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:21.250
And yeah, what else would you say about what we're doing here?
是的，对于我们在这里所做的事情，您还有什么想说的吗？

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.610
Well, first of all, I can't believe you only watched half of the episodes, I'm deeply offended.
好吧，首先，我不敢相信你只看了一半的剧集，我被深深冒犯了。

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.050
I think I'm just gonna walk off.
我想我要走开

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.410
I'm walking off the project.
我要离开这个项目了。

00:04:28.569 --> 00:04:34.170
No, the truth is, I haven't rewatched the show door to door since it went off.
不，事实是，自从节目结束后我就没有挨家挨户地重看过。

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.610
I've seen episodes, but I haven't watched the door to door.
我看过几集，但没挨家挨户看过。

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.769
And so I think what we're doing here is excavating back into our past.
所以我认为我们在这里所做的就是挖掘我们的过去。

00:04:40.769 --> 00:04:43.009
It was almost a decade of our lives.
这几乎是我们生命中的十年。

00:04:43.009 --> 00:04:46.569
And we're trying to figure out what did we do there?
我们试图弄清楚我们在那里做了什么？

00:04:46.569 --> 00:04:47.730
What happened?
发生了什么？

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.930
We made this thing.
我们做了这个东西。

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.490
It's like the pineapple episode.
这就像菠萝情节。

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.850
You're like, we have to piece it together.
你说，我们必须把它拼凑起来。

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.370
We're doing the pineapple incident.
我们正在处理菠萝事件。

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.810
but for the entire series, what happened?
但对于整个系列来说，发生了什么？

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:12.569
We woke up, we woke up, we were, we were waking up, we're almost 50 or I think you're, you're there and I'm almost there and we're kind of going, wait, we are closer to the age of future Ted, we are closer to 2030 than we were to do then we are to 2005 when the show launched.
我们醒了，我们醒了，我们醒了，我们快醒了，我们快50岁了，或者我想你快到了，我也快到了，我们正在走，等等，我们离未来特德的年龄更近了，我们比节目开播时的2005年更接近2030年。

00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:14.089
And it is just, it is strange.
这就是，这很奇怪。

00:05:14.089 --> 00:05:16.370
I was thinking about the sort of symmetry of it.
我在思考它的对称性。

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:23.370
We are something like, I think 20 years since the premiere, I think this September will be 20 years since the premiere.
我们就像是，我想自首映以来已有 20 年了，我认为今年 9 月将是自首映以来 20 年。

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:28.930
We are just past 10 years of the finale airing, a bit of finishing airing.
我们距离大结局播出已经过去了 10 年，算是收尾播出了。

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.490
So there's a lot of round numbers.
所以有很多整数。

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.089
There's a 20 and there's a 10 and here we are.
有一个 20，有一个 10，我们到了。

00:05:33.089 --> 00:05:37.170
And it just seems like a good moment to kind of look back and take stock of it.
这似乎是回顾和评估它的好时机。

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:47.769
Yeah, I, um, another thing that I, when I called you to talk about this, that I really wanted to talk about, I said, I am astonished one at the, the kind of long tail of the show.
是的，我，嗯，当我打电话给你谈论这个时，我真的很想谈论另一件事，我说，我对这部剧的长尾感到惊讶。

00:05:47.769 --> 00:05:59.709
You know, a lot of shows go off the air and, and they go off the air, they go away, you know, and maybe they come up randomly in a, I don't know, trivia night or a, you know, remember that a moment will come back to you.
你知道，很多节目都停播了，然后它们停播了，它们就消失了，你知道，也许它们会在一个我不知道的琐事之夜中随机出现，或者一个你知道的，记住某个时刻你会回来。

00:05:59.709 --> 00:06:02.339
But there's something about how I made Mother One.
但我是如何制作《母亲一号》的。

00:06:02.339 --> 00:06:05.060
It keeps minting new fans.
它不断地吸引新的粉丝。

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:11.540
So people that were babies, children, or even in their teens when it was on, have now discovered it.
因此，当它出现时，婴儿、儿童甚至青少年的人们现在都发现了它。

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.300
I also think there's a really sweet thing.
我也觉得有一个非常甜蜜的事情。

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.779
I think parents are showing it to their teenage kids now.
我认为父母现在正在向十几岁的孩子展示它。

00:06:15.779 --> 00:06:23.139
They're like, this show taught me a lot about being an adult or young adult navigating all these things.
他们就像，这个节目教会了我很多关于作为一个成年人或年轻人如何应对所有这些事情的知识。

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:35.060
But also, I'm astonished at a number of things, but one of the ones that strikes me about when I hear from how I made my mother fans, something I hear so consistently that it's not just anecdotal.
而且，我对很多事情感到惊讶，但其中一件让我震惊的是，当我听到我如何让我的母亲成为粉丝时，我一直听到这样的事情，这不仅仅是轶事。

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:53.139
It has to be, there has to be something there, which is that people say I got turned onto the show or I started watching the show when I was in a really hard moment of my life, whether it's, you know, I was going through a divorce or a sickness or my parent had died.
一定是这样，一定有什么东西，那就是人们说我开始看这个节目，或者我在人生中非常困难的时刻开始看这个节目，无论是，你知道，我正在经历离婚、生病还是我的父母去世了。

00:06:54.899 --> 00:07:06.680
I was having a personal kind of moment of crisis and there seems to be that this thing I've noticed that how I met your mother is like soul medicine for people going through hard times.
我正经历着个人的危机时刻，我注意到我如何遇见你母亲这件事似乎对于经历困难时期的人来说就像灵魂良药。

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:09.240
And I don't know that it was conceived of that.
我不知道它是这样构想的。

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.399
Exactly, I don't think you and Carter sat down in 2004 and said, I know what we'll do.
确切地说，我不认为你和卡特在 2004 年坐下来说，我知道我们会做什么。

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:17.360
We'll do a soul panacea for people.
我们将为人们做灵魂灵丹妙药。

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.639
But it seems like that's what it does for people.
但这似乎就是它对人们的作用。

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:25.199
And I hear it so consistently that it strikes me as something worth exploring.
我经常听到它，这让我觉得它是值得探索的东西。

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:26.199
It's such an honor.
真是太荣幸了。

00:07:26.199 --> 00:07:32.040
People come up to us all the time and to you, Josh, and say the show got them through something really hard.
人们总是来找我们，也来找你，乔什，说这部剧帮助他们度过了一些非常困难的时期。

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:38.279
And getting that, or they say I married my wife because we realized we're both how much mother fans.
得到这个，或者他们说我娶了我的妻子，因为我们意识到我们都是妈妈的粉丝。

00:07:38.279 --> 00:07:47.040
So they met in an event or something, like it's just the ways the show has been crucial in people's lives, like the opening words from the fans.
所以他们是在一次活动或其他事情中相遇的，就像这就是这部剧对人们生活至关重要的方式，就像粉丝们的开场白一样。

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.959
We have the greatest fans of any fans.
我们拥有所有粉丝中最伟大的粉丝。

00:07:48.959 --> 00:07:49.800
How much more the fans are?
粉丝还有多少？

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.800
Shout out to the fans.
向粉丝们喊话。

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:51.879
Huge shout out to the fans.
向粉丝们大声喊叫。

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:54.519
If you were listening to this, you were an amazing person.
如果你听到这个，你就是一个了不起的人。

00:07:54.519 --> 00:08:00.199
And I find such an openness, Josh, to come talk to us about stuff.
乔什，我发现自己很愿意来和我们谈论一些事情。

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:01.240
Do you get this?
你明白吗？

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:08.720
I get this a little bit because I'm a writer and people I have to go around telling people, I wear a little shirt that says I create a how much mother and just you got in that needy.
我有点明白这一点，因为我是一名作家，我必须到处告诉人们，我穿着一件小衬衫，上面写着我创造了一个母亲，你为那个有需要的人提供了多少。

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.240
But no one knows, I have a tattooed on my face.
但没有人知道，我脸上有纹身。

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.199
You have 10 most of me tattooed on your face.
你脸上纹了10个我的大部分。

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:26.959
And I've been dying for years to ask you, this sort of two-part question, what was it like being Ted when the show was on and blowing up and not being able to escape Ted's face, your face is dead space, although you are not Ted.
多年来我一直很想问你，这种由两部分组成的问题，当节目播出并爆炸时，作为泰德感觉如何，无法逃脱泰德的脸，你的脸是死气沉沉的空间，尽管你不是泰德。

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:33.360
And then, what does that felt like kind of in the long 10 years since it went off the air?
那么，自从它停播以来的漫长十年里，感觉怎么样？

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.643
What does that felt like?
那感觉怎么样？

00:08:34.643 --> 00:08:40.289
The reason I thought of that is that you just said people come up to you and they share these things with you.
我这么想的原因是你刚才说人们来找你并与你分享这些事情。

00:08:40.289 --> 00:08:41.726
That seems like a real gift.
这看起来像是一份真正的礼物。

00:08:41.726 --> 00:08:45.320
I'm sure there's also like like enormous, weird downsides, don't they?
我确信还有一些巨大的、奇怪的缺点，不是吗？

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.159
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:08:46.159 --> 00:08:47.000
Do it, do it.
做吧，做吧。

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:47.840
It's such an interesting thing.
这是一件非常有趣的事情。

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.240
Let's do a little tighter episode on being Ted Mosby.
让我们以泰德·莫斯比 (Ted Mosby) 的身份做一个更紧凑的剧集。

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:56.200
I think there's a lot to unpack that I wouldn't be able to unpack here, but I'll do a little bit of it.
我认为有很多东西需要解开，但我无法在这里解开，但我会做一些。

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.039
I will say this.
我会这么说。

00:08:57.039 --> 00:09:02.120
I remember I was writing liberal arts for the second film I wrote and directed.
我记得我正在为我自编自导的第二部电影撰写文科文章。

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.240
And it was 2009 or 10.
那是2009年或10年。

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.080
I think it was 2010.
我认为那是2010年。

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.779
And I went to Spain for a month.
我去了西班牙一个月。

00:09:08.779 --> 00:09:15.700
